course: dictionary
lesson: 14793
title: A steady beat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pulsation is a noun, and it means a regular beat or throb, like your heartbeat. «You can feel a pulsation in your wrist when your heart beats.» The key clue is regular: the beat comes again and again, at a steady pace.
explain: Pulsation also has a science meaning. «The star showed a slow pulsation, growing brighter, then dimmer, then brighter again.» Here the pulsation is a regular swelling and shrinking. The clues are brighter and dimmer, which show the change going back and forth.
explain: You can hear pulsation in music too. «The drummer kept a strong pulsation all through the song.» To check, ask: does this thing keep coming back in a steady rhythm? If it does, pulsation is a good fit.
fact: «Pulsation» means a regular beat or throb, like a heartbeat.
fact: In science, «pulsation» can mean a regular swelling and shrinking, such as a pulsating star.
fact: Your pulse is the pulsation you feel in your arteries with each heartbeat.
fact: In music, a pulsation is a strong, regular beat.
exercise: «You can feel a pulsation in your wrist.» What is a pulsation? | *A regular beat or throb, like a heartbeat | A loud shout | A type of wristwatch | A sudden silence
exercise: «The star's pulsation made it look brighter, then dimmer.» What does pulsation mean in this sentence? | A sudden silence | A long journey through space | *A regular swelling and shrinking | A bright colour
exercise: Find and copy the word that means a steady beat in this sentence: «The drummer kept a strong pulsation all through the song.» | *pulsation | drummer | song | strong
test: Your pulse is a pulsation in your arteries. What does that mean? | Hard to find under the skin | *A regular beat you can feel with each heartbeat | A bone in the arm | A type of blood
test: Which sentence uses pulsation correctly? | She put a pulsation on her bike | The pulsation of the sandwich was delicious | *The steady pulsation of the drum kept us dancing | I will pulsation the window shut
exam: In «The star had a slow pulsation, growing brighter, then dimmer», what does pulsation mean? | A dark cloud | A spinning top | *A regular swelling and shrinking | A sudden loud noise
